WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.383 --> 00:00:24.492
&gt;&gt; THIS MARKS THE 71st

00:00:24.493 --> 00:00:27.295
ANNIVERSARY OF D-DAY.

00:00:27.296 --> 00:00:28.596
WE'LL BE IN MORMA

00:00:28.597 --> 00:00:29.030
WE'LL BE IN MOR

00:00:29.031 --> 00:00:41.642
WE'LL BE IN NORMAN DAY DANDY.

00:00:41.643 --> 00:00:42.376
YOU'VE BEEN TALKING TO SOME OF

00:00:42.377 --> 00:00:43.111
THE WORLD WAR II VETERAN, WHAT

00:00:43.112 --> 00:00:43.544
DID YOU FIND?

00:00:43.545 --> 00:00:44.245
&gt;&gt; BEFORE WE FOUND THE UNITED

00:00:44.246 --> 00:00:44.979
STATES IN NEW ORLEANS, I SPOKE

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:45.446
TO BEN MARTINEZ.

00:00:45.447 --> 00:00:46.180
HE SIGNED UP TO SERVE IN WORLD

00:00:46.181 --> 00:00:46.848
WAR II, HE WAS 72 YEARS OLD.

00:00:46.849 --> 00:00:47.548
HE SERVED IN ITALY, WE TALKED

00:00:47.549 --> 00:00:48.282
ABOUT HOW D-DAY LET TO THE END

00:00:48.283 --> 00:00:48.983
OF THE THE WAR AND WHAT THAT

00:00:48.984 --> 00:00:52.120
MEANT TO HIM, WATCH.

00:00:52.121 --> 00:00:56.424
&gt;&gt; I WANTED TO GET IN RIGHT AWAY

00:00:56.425 --> 00:00:57.091
AT PEARL HARBOR, BUT I WAS

00:00:57.092 --> 00:00:57.558
ADVISED NOT TO.

00:00:57.559 --> 00:00:59.660
I HAD -- AND EVERYBODY SAID GET

00:00:59.661 --> 00:01:02.663
YOUR DEGREE FIRST AND THEN

00:01:02.664 --> 00:01:03.264
ENLIST.

00:01:03.265 --> 00:01:05.466
SO I ENLISTED IN MAY OF '42.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:08.002
GOT OUT IN THE MAY OF '46.

00:01:08.003 --> 00:01:11.205
&gt;&gt; BEN MARTINEZ SERVE IN THE

00:01:11.206 --> 00:01:11.873
ITALIAN CAMPAIGN AS A MEDIC.

00:01:11.874 --> 00:01:15.209
HE AND HIS TEAM TRAVERSED THE

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.044
ITALIAN ALPS WHILE A DONKEY

00:01:17.045 --> 00:01:18.746
CARRIED SUPPLIES.

00:01:18.747 --> 00:01:20.281
HE STILL REMEMBERS THE DAY HE

00:01:20.282 --> 00:01:21.582
RECEIVED WORD THAT THE WAR WAS

00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:28.156
OVER.

00:01:28.157 --> 00:01:30.124
&gt;&gt; WE WERE AT A LITTLE TOWN

00:01:30.125 --> 00:01:31.225
CALLED OGBOW.

00:01:31.226 --> 00:01:33.528
WE WERE LOADING UP THE MULE, WE

00:01:33.529 --> 00:01:36.531
WERE IN THE ALPS, WE WERE GOING

00:01:36.532 --> 00:01:41.736
TO GO UP HIGHER.

00:01:41.737 --> 00:01:43.604
WE WERE LOADING UP THE MULES

00:01:43.605 --> 00:01:45.406
WHEN THE WORD CAME DOWN, THE WAR

00:01:45.407 --> 00:01:46.607
WAS OVER.

00:01:46.608 --> 00:01:47.909
IT WAS COMPLETE SILENCE.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:48.876
NOBODY TALKED TO ANYBODY.

00:01:48.877 --> 00:01:57.919
I THINK THEY ALL HAD THEIR OWN

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:58.553
THING GOING ON.

00:01:58.554 --> 00:02:00.588
WHEN I CAME TO, MORE OR LESS,

00:02:00.589 --> 00:02:02.089
THE FIRST THING I DID WAS WENT

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:03.891
TO SEE THE MAN LOADING UP THE

00:02:03.892 --> 00:02:04.192
MULES.

00:02:04.193 --> 00:02:12.300
AND I THINK I STARTED CRYING.

00:02:12.301 --> 00:02:12.967
IT'S OVER.

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.202
YOU GUYS DON'T HAVE TO DO WHAT

00:02:14.203 --> 00:02:14.969
YOU DID BEFORE.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.137
IT'S OVER.

00:02:16.138 --> 00:02:23.211
&gt;&gt; BEN MARTINEZ CAME OVER AT THE

00:02:23.212 --> 00:02:26.113
SUMMER OF '45.

00:02:26.114 --> 00:02:28.549
AT NEARLY 100, HE VOLUNTEERS TWO

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:29.217
DAYS A WEEK AT THE NATIONAL

00:02:29.218 --> 00:02:30.284
WORLD WAR II MUSEUM IN NEW

00:02:30.285 --> 00:02:34.188
ORLEANS SHARING FIRSTHAND

00:02:34.189 --> 00:02:36.657
STORIES ONLY HE CAN TELL AND

00:02:36.658 --> 00:02:37.391
REMEMBERING THOSE WHO WERE NEVER

00:02:37.392 --> 00:02:38.059
ABLE TO TELL THEIR STORIES.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:38.826
&gt;&gt; LAURA, THAT IS WHAT WE WILL

00:02:38.827 --> 00:02:39.627
BE DOING THIS WEEK, TELLING THE

00:02:39.628 --> 00:02:41.729
STORIES OF THE CIVILIAN HEROES

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.565
WHO TRULY SAVED THE WORLD AS WE

00:02:44.566 --> 00:02:47.935
KNOW IT, THEIR WILLINGNESS TO

00:02:47.936 --> 00:02:48.903
SACRIFICE, THE COMMITMENT TO THE

00:02:48.904 --> 00:02:50.504
SHARED CAUSE IS SOMETHING WE

00:02:50.505 --> 00:02:51.572
LOST AND SOMETHING I HOPE TO

00:02:51.573 --> 00:02:55.876
REMIND THE YOUNG PEEP.

00:02:55.877 --> 00:02:56.644
&gt;&gt; THE YOUNG PEOPLE --

00:02:56.645 --> 00:03:03.150
&gt;&gt; WE KNOW THE STORIES, SO

00:03:03.151 --> 00:03:03.684
COMPELLING TO HEAR.

00:03:03.685 --> 00:03:04.385
BUT THE YOUNG PEOPLE, I HOPE,

00:03:04.386 --> 00:03:05.119
ARE GOING TO TAKE THE MOST OUT

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:05.820
OF THIS WEEK OF COMMEMORATION

00:03:05.821 --> 00:03:06.254
AND MEMORIES.

00:03:06.255 --> 00:03:06.854
THERE ARE NOT MANY LEFT.

00:03:06.855 --> 00:03:07.555
THIS WILL BE THE LAST MAJOR

00:03:07.556 --> 00:03:08.222
ANNIVERSARY TO CELEBRATE.

00:03:08.223 --> 00:03:14.962
I REMEMBER REAGAN DID THE

00:03:14.963 --> 00:03:21.569
SAME -- THE BOYS -- THEY TOOK

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:21.936
THE CLIP.

00:03:21.937 --> 00:03:22.270
&gt;&gt; YEAH.

00:03:22.271 --> 00:03:23.004
&gt;&gt; Laura: AND TOMORROW, WE'LL BE

00:03:23.005 --> 00:03:23.671
OUT ON THE STREETS WITH THE

00:03:23.672 --> 00:03:24.071
PROTESTERS.

00:03:24.072 --> 00:03:24.772
&gt;&gt; TODAY THE PROTESTERS WERE

00:03:24.773 --> 00:03:25.072
THIN.

00:03:25.073 --> 00:03:25.706
THERE WERE ONLY A HANDFUL

00:03:25.707 --> 00:03:27.108
OUTSIDE OF BUCKINGHAM PALACE.

00:03:27.109 --> 00:03:28.075
&gt;&gt; Laura: THERE THEY ARE.

00:03:28.076 --> 00:03:31.412
&gt;&gt; THOSE ARE THE TWO.

00:03:31.413 --> 00:03:33.381
IT WAS A THIN CROWD.

00:03:33.382 --> 00:03:34.115
TOMORROW THEY EXPECT THOUSANDS

00:03:34.116 --> 00:03:37.552
IN TRAFALGAR SQUARE.

